---
name: finite
---

# finite

Whether a float is finite — neither `NaN` nor an infinity. The test is
`x - x == 0.0`: subtraction of a finite value from itself is exactly
zero, while `NaN - NaN` and `Inf - Inf` are both `NaN`.

```soil-sig
finite : (x : F64) -> Bool
```

```test classifies
(1.0) => true
(-0.0) => true
("NaN") => false
("Inf") => false
("-Inf") => false
```
